+## Class and object facts area, 16 November 2026
+
+Area: class, object and method facts in `tcl-compiler` (class factories, definition scripts, method bodies, named instances, the lenient `tcl` environment's display facts, widget constructors as receivers). Measured with `cargo nextest run -p tcl-compiler`, test profile `opt-level 1`.
+
+| Point | Run | Failing | `class_factories` |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Baseline at `c8099ccc` | 13,123 | 2,355 | 50 |
+| First batch on that base | 13,123 | 2,352 (fixed 3, new 0) | 48 |
+| `a2df29e1` (first batch pushed; other sessions' fixes included) | 13,129 | 2,247 | 48 |
+| Second batch on `a2df29e1` | 13,130 | see the push report | 44 |
+
+Fixed:
+
+- **A class declared in a `namespace eval` body was invisible afterwards.** The source advice merged every body's effects as a possibility, so `namespace eval ::n {oo::class create C {method m {} {}}}; ::n::C create x; x nosuch` had no class cell at the top level: no instance, no W308, no class made by a metaclass declared in a namespace. A literal namespace body runs once in its command's invocation, so its command world is the enclosing script's own (`BodyWalk::regions`, Native policy only). The body walk also answers a class-relation query for a parent it retains, and a TclOO definer whose script only declares members leaves no blanket footprint inside a body, as at the top level. `c_source_namespace_class_after_unentered_definition_body_keeps_unknown_mutation` expected an unknown mutation after a members-only class body; tclsh 8.6.18 and 9.0.4 change nothing but the class, so only its `uplevel` row keeps the obligation.
+- **Named-instance display labels** (`OriginalProjectClassCards::named_instance_display_reports`) were withheld for any document that constructs an object, because each construction marks the catalogue as following an unread operation. A label now needs only that every unread operation is a construction of, or a call on, a source class of the catalogue (`labels_complete`); class cards keep the strict flag. Decision taken under the display and proof policy.
+- **`instance_classes` under the lenient `tcl` input** reads the retained logical constructor shape and class declaration.
+- **A class-declared variable in an uncalled method, constructor or destructor body** was a fresh local that is definitely unset, so `$_x` was a proved error and every later read of the body was dropped. `seed_declared_receiver_variables` (`command_binding/receiver_self.rs`, called from `seed_deferred_inputs`) makes the declared names cells of the declaring class with unknown contents, shared by its bodies; a formal of the same name keeps its slot. tclsh 8.6.18, 9.0.4 and 9.1.0 records are on `it_4 analyser::method_bodies::a_class_variable_is_object_state_in_every_body_of_its_class`.
+- **A store to object storage is not W211 or W220** (`written_object_storage`): another body of the object reads it.
+- **A bodiless member flagged the module as holding unretained executable roots** (`Lowerer::extract_one_member`), which marks every binding of the file opaque. `variable` and `superclass` have no body word.
+- **The workspace factory index under a pinned release.** `class_factory_for_command` read the index only for a logical input. `analyser/workspace_class_factory.rs` reads it when the head is a written word absent from the document's closed command world, through the head's ordered lookup candidates.
+
+Open, with the cause where it is established:
+
+- **A relative head in a TclOO method body** (`method m {} {return $neverBound}`): the unit is `trivial_guarded` whenever the body's namespace is runtime-selected and any head is relative (`build_method_units`, `requires_runtime_command_namespace`), so no flow diagnostic runs. An uncalled body already resolves such heads through the receiver path when the command world is known (`original_receiver_command_lookup`). Asked the analyser and binding session whether an uncalled receiver method may be read against the fresh-receiver path in the end-of-load world.
+- **TclOO creation under a namespace that does not exist** (`oo::class create ::nope::X {…}`) withdraws the command world; tclsh 8.6.18, 9.0.4 and 9.1.0 create every missing namespace. Handed to the analyser and binding session. It starves `a_metaclass_file_publishes_exactly_one_factory` and the cross-file tests that read `META_FILE`.
+- **Every command after `oo::define C {…}` or `oo::define C method …` is unknown** (item 2). `oo::class create` takes the preserving-publication route (`PreservingCommandPublication`, `definition_has_only_deferred_members`); `oo::define` has no counterpart, so its script is entered as an ordinary body where `method` fails the compile preflight, and the command world is unclosed for the rest of the file (no W308, no typed call). Not started.
+- **`next` in an entered TclOO method body draws W123**: the presence query looks the head up from `::` without `::oo::Helpers`. Handed to the analyser and binding session; keeps `a_provably_direct_body_keeps_method_checks_live` failing.
+- **A class made by a user metaclass has no relation providers**, so it never publishes a factory of its own (`a_computed_metaclass_name_resolves_through_a_literal_call_site`, the replayed-creation tests): its definition body has no owner, because `original_class_definition_body_in_analysis` requires a registry definer's body grammar at the creation call.
+- Not started: registry widget constructors as receivers (item 6), `package require Tk` under a logical input (item 5), the clay inventory tests.
+
